              {
                "detail": "The core SERP, Keepa enrichment, report generation, and optional public upload flow matches the stated Amazon market-analysis purpose, but the root skill also adds an expert-skill-creator self-extension path that is broader than market analysis.",
                "label": "Purpose & Capability",
                "name": "purpose_capability",
                "rating": "concern"
              }
            ],
            "guidance": "Install only if you trust the LinkFox service boundary and can control the runtime environment. Avoid endpoint override variables unless you are deliberately testing against a trusted host, do not store API keys in shell profiles if a credential manager or session-scoped variable is available, review any feedback or public upload before sending, and treat generated HTML reports as active content when opening or sharing them.",
            "findings": "[TT3] unexpected: Sending an API key to LinkFox services is expected, but the artifacts support the concern that LINKFOX_TOOL_GATEWAY and related environment variables can redirect credential-bearing auth and gateway traffic without destination validation.\n[T09] unexpected: The static endpoint-override finding is supported by onboarding.py and gateway scripts that combine environment-selected base URLs with phone numbers, SMS codes, access tokens, refresh tokens, API keys, and Authorization headers.\n[T01] unexpected: The automatic feedback instruction is supported and is not necessary for completing Amazon search or market analysis; it can transmit user statements or inferred intent to a separate feedback endpoint without explicit per-send consent.\n[T09] unexpected: The report generator finding is supported: inject_report.py directly inserts HTML content and extracted ECharts/Canvas JavaScript into the generated report, which is risky if product data, model output, or fragments are attacker-influenced.\n[T09] unexpected: The plaintext API-key persistence finding is supported by onboarding.md commands that append LINKFOX_AGENT_API_KEY to shell startup files or Windows user environment variables.\n[T08] unexpected: The dependency finding is supported by install guidance for unpinned packages; no evidence showed those packages are malicious, so this is a supply-chain hygiene concern rather than a malicious indicator.\n[TP4] expected: Public upload is disclosed by the file-upload skill and the root skill says to use it when a public download link is requested; this is purpose-aligned but users should confirm the content is safe to publish.\n[SDI-2] unexpected: The self-extension instruction to use expert-skill-creator for adding or modifying capabilities is materially broader than the declared SERP market-structure analysis role.\n[SDI-1] expected: The AIGC companion is referenced by the root skill for main-image understanding, so the separate AIGC documentation is not inherently mismatched, though its onboarding and endpoint behavior contributes to the credential-handling concerns.",
